  "answer": "I'll start by exploring the workspace and running the existing test.\nNow let me run the existing test to confirm the failure.\nTest passes. Quick extra sanity check on edge cases (without touching the test files):\nDone. Repair verified.\n\n**What I did**\n\n1. **Ran the existing test first** (`bun test`) to confirm the failure: `tokens('')` returned `[\"\"]` instead of `[]`, since the original implementation was just `value.split(',')` — no trimming, no empty removal.\n\n2. **Repaired `src/tokens.ts`** with a minimal change, preserving the signature `export function tokens(value: string)`:\n   ```ts\n   export function tokens(value: string) {\n     return value\n       .split(',')\n       .map((token) => token.trim())\n       .filter((token) => token.length > 0)\n   }\n   ```\n   Each comma-separated token is trimmed, then zero-length tokens are dropped.\n\n3. **Verified the repair**:\n   - `bun test` → **1 pass, 0 fail** (3 `expect()` calls), up from 0 pass / 1 fail.\n   - Extra ad-hoc edge-case check via a throwaway `bun -e` command (no files added): `''`, `'  '`, and `','` all → `[]`; `' a, ,b ,,c '` → `[\"a\",\"b\",\"c\"]`; `'single'` → `[\"single\"]`; `'a,b'` → `[\"a\",\"b\"]`.\n\n**Untouched, per AGENTS.md:** `AGENTS.md`, `package.json`, and `test/oracle.test.ts` remain byte-for-byte as they were; no configuration files added and no change to the test runner (still `bun:test`). The only file modified is `src/tokens.ts`."
